# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore
# =============================================================================
# WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS:
#   Everything not excluded here is uploaded to the Docker daemon as build
#   context before a single instruction runs. Without this file that is
#   venv/ (2.3 GB) plus data/ (5 GB) plus .git — around 8 GB copied on every
#   build, to produce an image that needs none of it.
#
#   Artifacts are mounted as volumes at runtime, never baked in, so excluding
#   them here is not a compromise — it is the design.
# =============================================================================

# --- Virtual environments (rebuilt inside the image) ---
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Data: 5 GB, and mounted as a volume at runtime ---
data/raw/
data/processed/
# data/sample/ is deliberately NOT excluded — it is small, committed, and
# what the test suite runs against.

# --- Model artifacts: mounted as a volume so a retrain is not a rebuild ---
models/*.keras
models/*.h5
models/*.pkl
models/*.joblib
models/*.state.json

# --- Version control and CI ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# --- Python bytecode and tooling caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Logs ---
logs/
*.log

# --- Secrets: must never enter an image layer ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Docs and notebooks (not needed at runtime) ---
docs/
notebooks/
*.md
!README.md

# --- Editor / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- Docker's own files ---
docker/
